 1)When we use const constructors in Flutter, the app becomes a little faster and smoother while scrolling.Why?

   Ans -> Because Flutter does not need to create the same widget again and again every time the screen rebuilds.
          Normally, when scrolling happens, Flutter rebuilds many widgets.
  
 2)Explain why InheritedWidget (or Provider) outperforms "lifting state up" forcross-tab data.

   Ans -> When we use “lifting state up”, we keep the data in a parent widget and pass it down to many child widgets using constructors.
          This works fine for small apps.But in bigger apps, especially with multiple tabs, it becomes slow and messy.
          Because every time the data changes, many widgets rebuild again — even widgets that don’t need the update.

 3)Explain the difference between MainAxisAlignment and CrossAxisAlignment in a Row.

   Ans -> In a Row, there are 2 directions:

          Horizontal direction → called the main axis
          Vertical direction → called the cross axis

          So:
 
         MainAxisAlignment controls widgets left and right
         CrossAxisAlignment controls widgets up and down.
  
 4)Explain why a Stack widget is used for overlaying UI elements.
 

   Ans -> A Stack widget in Flutter is used when we want to place widgets on top of each other (overlay).

         Normally, widgets in Row or Column are arranged side by side or one below another.

         But sometimes we need designs like:

         text on an image
         button over a photo
         notification badge on an icon
         loading spinner over screen

         That is where Stack is useful. 

 5)Explain the role of ValueKey when reordering items in a list.

   Ans -> ValueKey helps Flutter identify widgets correctly when items in a list change position or get reordered.
  
          Without keys, Flutter can get confused.
  
          It may think:
     
          “This is the same widget, just moved.”
  
          Because of that:
 
          wrong data can appear
          UI state can mix up
          animations may behave strangely
